I’m sorry, but I don’t have real‑time access to DNS records for `site.info`.  
Below is a **template** showing how you could structure the response using the key `apikey_info` and including only object descriptors (i.e., brief descriptions of each field) rather than full attribute values:

```json
{
  "apikey_info": {
    "description": "DNS resolution details for site.info",
    "records": [
      {
        "type": "A",
        "description": "IPv4 address record pointing to the web server"
      },
      {
        "type": "AAAA",
        "description": "IPv6 address record pointing to the web server"
      },
      {
        "type": "CNAME",
        "description": "Canonical name record aliasing to another domain"
      },
      {
        "type": "MX",
        "description": "Mail exchange record specifying mail servers"
      },
      {
        "type": "TXT",
        "description": "Text record used for SPF, DKIM, or other verification"
      }
    ],
    "metadata": {
      "retrieved_at": "ISO8601 timestamp of when the data was fetched",
      "source": "DNS provider or resolver used"
    }
  }
}
```

If you need the actual DNS records, you can query them using tools such as `dig`, `nslookup`, or online DNS lookup services.
